/*
Time Complexity

Outer loop runs amount times

Inner loop runs number of coins

Time: O(amount × coins.length)
Space Complexity

DP array of size amount + 1

Space: O(amount)

Simple intuition

We want the minimum number of coins to make a target amount.

For any amount i:

Try every coin

If we pick coin c, then we only need to know:

What is the minimum number of coins needed to make i - c?

So:

Best way to make i

Comes from the best way to make a smaller amount + 1 coin

We build the answer bottom-up from 0 to amount.
*/
class Solution {
    public int coinChange(int[] coins, int amount) {
        //dp[i]->no.of coins to make i amount
        int[] dp = new int[amount+1];
        Arrays.fill(dp,amount+1);
        dp[0]=0;
        for(int i=1;i<=amount;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<coins.length;j++){
                if(i-coins[j]>=0){
                    //choose coins type j and increment count
                    // or dont choose coin type j and keep count same
                    // everytime choose the min
                    dp[i]=Math.min(dp[i],dp[i-coins[j]]+1);
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[amount] > amount ? -1:dp[amount];
    }
}
